}

steps.body:
Both loops work on a `List` too. The index form uses `size()` and `get(i)`. For-each works the same as with arrays:

```java norun
for (int i = 0; i < list.size(); i++) {
    System.out.println(list.get(i));
}
for (int x : list) { ... }     // unboxes each Integer
for (Integer x : list) { ... } // keeps the wrapper
```

`for (int x : list)` throws `NullPointerException` if the list holds a `null`, so use `Integer` when nulls are possible.

Never call `list.remove` or `list.add` inside a for-each over that same list. The loop's next pass usually throws `ConcurrentModificationException`, and when it does not, it silently skips elements. To remove while looping, use an `Iterator` (`import java.util.Iterator;`):

```java harness
import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        List<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>(List.of(3, -1, 4, -5, 9));
        {{code}}
        System.out.println(list);
    }
}
```

```java
Iterator<Integer> it = list.iterator();
while (it.hasNext()) {
    int x = it.next();
    if (x < 0) {
        it.remove(); // removes x safely
    }
}
```

`hasNext()` asks if another element is left, `next()` returns it and moves on, and `it.remove()` deletes the element `next()` just returned. Call `next()` exactly once per pass, and `it.remove()` at most once after it.

example.code:
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Iterator;
import java.util.List;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Integer> prices = new ArrayList<>(List.of(12, 3, 8, 4, 20));

        int total = 0;
        for (int price : prices) {
            total += price;
        }
        System.out.println("Total: " + total);

        for (int i = 0; i < prices.size(); i++) {
            System.out.println((i + 1) + ": " + prices.get(i));
        }

        Iterator<Integer> it = prices.iterator();
        while (it.hasNext()) {
            int price = it.next();
            if (price < 5) {
                it.remove();
            }
        }
        System.out.println("Kept: " + prices);
    }
}

